{
  "assessment": "The source provides a quantitative model for the static rolling friction of liquid marbles, with two regimes (large and small marbles) and a logistic function for the surface-fraction dependence. The extraction focuses on the large-marble regime (Eq. 2) and the small-marble regime (Eq. 3), both using the same controls (volume Ω and surface fraction φ) and readout (departure angle α). The model parameters μ, f(φ_o), a(φ_o), and β are supported by the text. The case is authoring-ready because it includes numeric controls, readouts, mechanisms, and quantitative claims with explicit domains.",
  "case_authoring_ready": true,
  "source": {
    "citation": "Yui Takai, Static Friction of Liquid Marbles, Physical Review Letters (2026), DOI:10.1103/njnj-yhc6",
    "journal_doi": "10.1103/njnj-yhc6",
    "arxiv_versioned_id": "2506.20116v2"
  },
  "paper_scope": "The paper measures and models the static rolling friction of liquid marbles (water droplets coated with lycopodium particles) on tilted substrates. It derives departure angle α as a function of marble volume Ω and particle surface fraction φ, using a granular-raft shear-yielding model. Two regimes are modeled: large gravity-flattened marbles (Eq. 2) and small quasi-spherical marbles (Eq. 3). The surface-fraction dependence is captured by a logistic function f(φ) with parameters β and φ_c. The paper also validates the logistic form with independent granular-raft force measurements, but the selected cluster focuses on the marble departure-angle data.",
  "mechanisms": [
    {
      "mechanism_id": "large_marble_model",
      "statement": "For large marbles (Ω > 7 μL), gravity flattens the marble to a height ~2a, and the departure angle α is given by Eq. (2): α ≈ (1/2)(1 + sqrt(8π a^3/Ω)) μ f(φ)/(1-f(φ)), where a is the capillary length, μ is the macroscopic friction coefficient, and f(φ) is the dimensionless intergrain force function.",
      "equations": [
        "α ≈ (1/2)(1 + sqrt(8π a^3/Ω)) μ f(φ)/(1-f(φ))"
      ],
      "variable_names": ["α", "Ω", "a", "μ", "f(φ)"],
      "parameters": [
        {
          "name": "mu_large",
          "value": 0.053,
          "uncertainty": "±0.003 (standard error, source_unspecified)",
          "unit": "dimensionless",
          "role": "macroscopic friction coefficient of the granular shell",
          "anchors": [
            {
              "line_start": 115,
              "line_end": 115,
              "support": "Fitting Eq. (2) in the large-marble regime with f(φ_o)=0.26 and a(φ_o)≈2.3 mm gives μ=0.053±0.003."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "f_phi_o",
          "value": 0.26,
          "uncertainty": "not reported",
          "unit": "dimensionless",
          "role": "dimensionless intergrain force function at initial surface fraction φ_o",
          "anchors": [
            {
              "line_start": 115,
              "line_end": 115,
              "support": "Fitting Eq. (2) with f(φ_o)=0.26."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "a_phi_o",
          "value": 0.0023,
          "uncertainty": "not reported",
          "unit": "m",
          "role": "capillary length at φ_o, corresponding to γ_eff(φ_o)≈53 mN/m",
          "anchors": [
            {
              "line_start": 115,
              "line_end": 115,
              "support": "a(φ_o)≈2.3 mm, i.e. γ_eff(φ_o)≈53 mN/m."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "anchors": [
        {
          "line_start": 105,
          "line_end": 113,
          "support": "Derivation of Eq. (2) for large marbles: height ~2a, cylindrical shape, S≈πl^2/2+2πla, δϵ≈δx/2a, leading to α≈(1/2)(1+sqrt(8πa^3/Ω)) μ f/(1-f)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "mechanism_id": "small_marble_model",
      "statement": "For small quasi-spherical marbles (Ω < ~15 μL), the departure angle α is given by Eq. (3): α ≈ (6π^2)^{1/3} (a^3/Ω)^{2/3} μ f(φ)/(1-f(φ)), with shear confined near the contact region.",
      "equations": [
        "α ≈ (6π^2)^{1/3} (a^3/Ω)^{2/3} μ f(φ)/(1-f(φ))"
      ],
      "variable_names": ["α", "Ω", "a", "μ", "f(φ)"],
      "parameters": [
        {
          "name": "small_prefactor",
          "value": 0.69,
          "uncertainty": "not reported",
          "unit": "dimensionless",
          "role": "empirical prefactor adjusting Eq. (3) to match small-Ω data",
          "anchors": [
            {
              "line_start": 122,
              "line_end": 122,
              "support": "Using μ obtained for large marbles, Eq. (3) predicts the small-Ω data with a prefactor of 0.69."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "anchors": [
        {
          "line_start": 117,
          "line_end": 121,
          "support": "Derivation of Eq. (3) for small marbles: l~R^2/a, S≈2πRl, δϵ≈δx/l, leading to α≈(6π^2)^{1/3}(a^3/Ω)^{2/3} μ f/(1-f)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "mechanism_id": "logistic_f_phi",
      "statement": "The dimensionless intergrain force function f(φ) follows a logistic function: f(φ) = 1/(1+exp[-β(φ-φ_c)]), with φ_c ≈ 0.90 ± 0.01 and β = 15.4 ± 1.7 for liquid marbles. This function emerges from the particle network approaching percolation and saturating near close packing.",
      "equations": [
        "f(φ) = 1/(1+exp[-β(φ-φ_c)])",
        "φ_c = φ_o - (1/β) ln(γ/γ_eff(φ_o) - 1)"
      ],
      "variable_names": ["f(φ)", "φ", "β", "φ_c", "φ_o", "γ", "γ_eff"],
      "parameters": [
        {
          "name": "beta_marble",
          "value": 15.4,
          "uncertainty": "±1.7 (source_unspecified)",
          "unit": "dimensionless",
          "role": "steepness parameter of the logistic function for liquid marbles",
          "anchors": [
            {
              "line_start": 139,
              "line_end": 139,
              "support": "Best exponential fit exp[β(φ-φ_o)] with β=15.4±1.7."
            },
            {
              "line_start": 155,
              "line_end": 155,
              "support": "Data collapse onto α/α_o = exp[β(φ-φ_o)] with β=15.4±1.7."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "phi_c_marble",
          "value": 0.9,
          "uncertainty": "±0.01 (source_unspecified)",
          "unit": "dimensionless",
          "role": "inflection point of the logistic function for liquid marbles",
          "anchors": [
            {
              "line_start": 164,
              "line_end": 164,
              "support": "φ_c ≈ 0.90 ± 0.01."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "anchors": [
        {
          "line_start": 159,
          "line_end": 164,
          "support": "From experimental result and Eq. (2) in asymptotic limit, f(φ) = 1/(1+exp[-β(φ-φ_c)]) with φ_c = φ_o - (1/β)ln(γ/γ_eff(φ_o)-1), giving φ_c≈0.90±0.01."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "fixed_conditions": [
    {
      "condition_id": "substrate_independent",
      "statement": "Static friction is substrate-independent; measurements are averaged over hydrophilic, hydrophobic, and superhydrophobic substrates.",
      "anchors": [
        {
          "line_start": 75,
          "line_end": 75,
          "support": "Static friction is substrate-independent despite differences in wetting and roughness."
        },
        {
          "line_start": 115,
          "line_end": 115,
          "support": "Departure angle averaged over the three substrates since static friction is substrate-independent."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "condition_id": "lycopodium_particles",
      "statement": "Marbles are coated with lycopodium particles of mean diameter d=32±3 μm, with initial surface fraction φ_o=0.83±0.01.",
      "anchors": [
        {
          "line_start": 62,
          "line_end": 62,
          "support": "Lycopodium particles have mean diameter d=32 μm with standard deviation 3 μm, and initial surface fraction φ_o=0.83±0.01."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "condition_id": "water_properties",
      "statement": "Water drops have surface tension γ=72 mN/m and density ρ=1000 kg/m^3.",
      "anchors": [
        {
          "line_start": 62,
          "line_end": 62,
          "support": "Water drops of surface tension γ=72 mN/m, density ρ=1000 kg/m^3."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "condition_id": "quasi_static_tilting",
      "statement": "Substrate is tilted at a typical angular speed ~2×10^-3 rad/s until the marble starts moving; viscous effects are negligible (viscous number J≈10^-7).",
      "anchors": [
        {
          "line_start": 503,
          "line_end": 503,
          "support": "Tilted at typical angular speed ~2×10^-3 rad/s; viscous number J≈10^-7≪1."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "controls": [
    {
      "name": "marble_volume",
      "definition": "Initial volume of the liquid marble, varied from 1.5 to 300 μL in the first experiment.",
      "unit": "μL",
      "minimum": 1.5,
      "maximum": 300,
      "anchors": [
        {
          "line_start": 74,
          "line_end": 74,
          "support": "We vary the marble initial volume from 1.5 to 300 μL and measure static friction F on each substrate."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "surface_fraction",
      "definition": "Particle surface fraction φ of the marble shell, varied by adding or removing water at fixed particle number, for initial volumes Ω_o=50–150 μL.",
      "unit": "dimensionless",
      "minimum": 0.7,
      "maximum": 1.0,
      "anchors": [
        {
          "line_start": 145,
          "line_end": 147,
          "support": "S is varied by adding or removing water; φ=(S_o/S)φ_o. Figure F3b shows φ versus δΩ/Ω_o for Ω_o=50–150 μL."
        },
        {
          "line_start": 156,
          "line_end": 156,
          "support": "Departure angle increases from less than 0.8% for inflated marbles with φ~0.7 to more than 50% for deflated marbles with φ close to 1."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "readouts": [
    {
      "name": "departure_angle",
      "definition": "The slope angle α at which the marble starts moving on a tilted substrate, measured with a digital goniometer. It corresponds to the friction-to-weight ratio.",
      "unit": "rad",
      "statistic": "Averaged over three substrates (hydrophilic, hydrophobic, superhydrophobic) for the volume dependence; individual measurements for the surface-fraction dependence.",
      "uncertainty": "Not explicitly reported for individual measurements; 95% confidence intervals shown in figures.",
      "resolution": null,
      "anchors": [
        {
          "line_start": 63,
          "line_end": 63,
          "support": "α is the slope at which the tangential weight F=ρΩg sinα overcomes static friction, measured with a digital goniometer."
        },
        {
          "line_start": 115,
          "line_end": 115,
          "support": "Departure angle averaged over the three substrates."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "claims": [
    {
      "claim_id": "large_marble_alpha",
      "statement": "For large marbles (Ω > 7 μL), the departure angle α is predicted by α ≈ (1/2)(1 + sqrt(8π a^3/Ω)) μ f(φ)/(1-f(φ)), with fitted parameters μ=0.053±0.003, f(φ_o)=0.26, a(φ_o)=2.3 mm. The model agrees with data over two decades in volume from 3 to 300 μL.",
      "quantitative_form": "α ≈ (1/2)(1 + sqrt(8π a^3/Ω)) μ f(φ)/(1-f(φ))",
      "mechanism_ids": ["large_marble_model"],
      "control_names": ["marble_volume"],
      "control_domains": [
        {
          "control_name": "marble_volume",
          "minimum": 3,
          "maximum": 300,
          "anchors": [
            {
              "line_start": 115,
              "line_end": 115,
              "support": "The model agrees with the data over two decades in volume, from 3 to 300 μL."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "readout_names": ["departure_angle"],
      "fixed_condition_ids": ["substrate_independent", "lycopodium_particles", "water_properties", "quasi_static_tilting"],
      "applicability": "Large-marble regime where gravity flattens the marble to height ~2a; valid for Ω>7 μL, with agreement down to 3 μL.",
      "statistical_basis": "Fitted to averaged data over three substrates; 95% confidence intervals shown in Fig. F2c.",
      "uncertainty": "μ=0.053±0.003; other parameters fixed without reported uncertainty.",
      "depends_on": [],
      "anchors": [
        {
          "line_start": 115,
          "line_end": 115,
          "support": "Fitting Eq. (2) in the large-marble regime with f(φ_o)=0.26 and a(φ_o)≈2.3 mm gives μ=0.053±0.003; model agrees with data from 3 to 300 μL."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "small_marble_alpha",
      "statement": "For small quasi-spherical marbles, the departure angle α is predicted by α ≈ (6π^2)^{1/3} (a^3/Ω)^{2/3} μ f(φ)/(1-f(φ)), using the same μ as for large marbles, adjusted by a prefactor of 0.69. The model remains valid up to ~15 μL.",
      "quantitative_form": "α ≈ (6π^2)^{1/3} (a^3/Ω)^{2/3} μ f(φ)/(1-f(φ))",
      "mechanism_ids": ["small_marble_model"],
      "control_names": ["marble_volume"],
      "control_domains": [
        {
          "control_name": "marble_volume",
          "minimum": 3,
          "maximum": 15,
          "anchors": [
            {
              "line_start": 122,
              "line_end": 123,
              "support": "The small-marble model remains valid up to ~15 μL; for 3≲Ω≲15 μL both models describe the data."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "readout_names": ["departure_angle"],
      "fixed_condition_ids": ["substrate_independent", "lycopodium_particles", "water_properties", "quasi_static_tilting"],
      "applicability": "Small-marble regime where marbles are quasi-spherical; valid up to ~15 μL.",
      "statistical_basis": "Prediction using μ from large marbles; prefactor 0.69 accounts for geometry-dependent approximations.",
      "uncertainty": "Prefactor 0.69 without reported uncertainty; μ uncertainty as above.",
      "depends_on": ["large_marble_alpha"],
      "anchors": [
        {
          "line_start": 122,
          "line_end": 122,
          "support": "Using μ obtained for large marbles, Eq. (3) predicts the small-Ω data with a prefactor of 0.69."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "logistic_alpha_phi",
      "statement": "The departure angle α increases exponentially with surface fraction φ: α/α_o = exp[β(φ-φ_o)] with β=15.4±1.7, for initial volumes Ω_o=50–150 μL. This corresponds to f(φ) following a logistic function.",
      "quantitative_form": "α/α_o = exp[β(φ-φ_o)]",
      "mechanism_ids": ["logistic_f_phi"],
      "control_names": ["surface_fraction"],
      "control_domains": [
        {
          "control_name": "surface_fraction",
          "minimum": 0.7,
          "maximum": 1.0,
          "anchors": [
            {
              "line_start": 156,
              "line_end": 156,
              "support": "Departure angle increases from less than 0.8% for φ~0.7 to more than 50% for φ close to 1."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "readout_names": ["departure_angle"],
      "fixed_condition_ids": ["substrate_independent", "lycopodium_particles", "water_properties", "quasi_static_tilting"],
      "applicability": "Marbles with initial volumes Ω_o=50–150 μL; surface fraction varied by adding/removing water.",
      "statistical_basis": "Data for all initial volumes collapse onto the exponential fit; β=15.4±1.7.",
      "uncertainty": "β=15.4±1.7; α_o is the departure angle at φ_o.",
      "depends_on": [],
      "anchors": [
        {
          "line_start": 155,
          "line_end": 155,
          "support": "Data for all initial volumes collapse onto α/α_o = exp[β(φ-φ_o)] with β=15.4±1.7."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_ambiguities": [
    {
      "ambiguity_id": "uncertainty_interpretation",
      "statement": "The reported uncertainties (e.g., μ=0.053±0.003, β=15.4±1.7, φ_c=0.90±0.01) are not explicitly defined as standard errors or confidence intervals; the source does not specify the convention.",
      "claim_ids": ["large_marble_alpha", "small_marble_alpha", "logistic_alpha_phi"],
      "mechanism_ids": ["large_marble_model", "small_marble_model", "logistic_f_phi"],
      "control_names": ["marble_volume", "surface_fraction"],
      "readout_names": ["departure_angle"],
      "fixed_condition_ids": ["substrate_independent", "lycopodium_particles", "water_properties", "quasi_static_tilting"],
      "anchors": [
        {
          "line_start": 115,
          "line_end": 115,
          "support": "μ=0.053±0.003."
        },
        {
          "line_start": 139,
          "line_end": 139,
          "support": "β=15.4±1.7."
        },
        {
          "line_start": 164,
          "line_end": 164,
          "support": "φ_c≈0.90±0.01."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "ambiguity_id": "small_prefactor_origin",
      "statement": "The prefactor 0.69 for the small-marble model is described as 'close to unity and accounting for geometry-dependent approximations', but its exact derivation is not provided.",
      "claim_ids": ["small_marble_alpha"],
      "mechanism_ids": ["small_marble_model"],
      "control_names": ["marble_volume"],
      "readout_names": ["departure_angle"],
      "fixed_condition_ids": ["substrate_independent", "lycopodium_particles", "water_properties", "quasi_static_tilting"],
      "anchors": [
        {
          "line_start": 122,
          "line_end": 122,
          "support": "Eq. (3) predicts the small-Ω data with a prefactor of 0.69, close to unity and accounting for geometry-dependent approximations."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
